<div class="drillui-bar">

<$edit-text tiddler="$:/drillui/bridge/draft" tag="input" default="" placeholder="https://…/server/8787/  — the bridge base URL" class="drillui-url"/><$button tooltip="point the frame at this URL — this restarts the REPL session"><$action-setfield $tiddler="$:/drillui/bridge" text={{$:/drillui/bridge/draft}}/>load</$button><$button tooltip="reload the frame: the bridge kills the REPL process and spawns a new one"><$action-setfield $tiddler="$:/drillui/bridge" text=""/><$action-setfield $tiddler="$:/drillui/bridge" text={{$:/drillui/bridge/draft}}/>reload ⟳</$button><a href={{$:/drillui/bridge}} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="drillui-tab">tab ↗</a>

</div>

<$reveal type="nomatch" state="$:/drillui/bridge" text="">
<iframe class="drillui-frame" src={{$:/drillui/bridge}} frameborder="0" marginwidth="0" marginheight="0" allow="clipboard-read; clipboard-write"></iframe>
</$reveal>

<$reveal type="match" state="$:/drillui/bridge" text="">

<div class="drillui-blank">

No bridge URL set. Enter the URL where `bun run tools/drillui_bridge.ts` serves its terminal page — the same URL you would open in a browser tab — and press ''load''.

* local: `http://localhost:8787/`
* CoCalc: `https://cocalc.ai/<project-id>/server/8787/`

If the panel stays blank //after// loading, the frame was refused: press ''tab ↗'', which shows the error a frame swallows. An https wiki cannot embed an `http://` bridge at all — use the proxied `https://` URL.

</div>

</$reveal>

<div class="drillui-foot">

One frame == one REPL process: `drillui_bridge.ts` spawns it on WebSocket open and kills it on close. Closing this tiddler, or pressing ''load'' / ''reload'', ends the running session.

</div>
